WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.390 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  once upon a time on the island of sicily  there was a race that ran right through  your village  [Music]  it was glorious it was beautiful it was  clearly planned before safety was a  consideration  [Music]  the targer florio was founded in sicily  by a speed loving fellow named vincenzio  florio in 1906 and it enthralled the  racing world for decades to come  but this was no ordinary race it took  place in the mountains outside of  palermo racers encountered bandits  wolves 500-plus hairpin turns on roads  that hadn't changed since togas were in  fashion  the course went straight through towns  and villages with no barricades or  warnings  the first year a driver named alessandro  cagno won it took him nine hours and his  average speed was 30 miles an hour  the targa florio ran for 71 years titans  of the car world like mario andretti  competed but a growing realization that  the race was crazy dangerous led to it  being shut down in 1977  it was the longest running car race in  the world at the time  today the grandstand outside palermo  sits empty  but evidence of the race is everywhere  peaking out in the beautiful landscape  the targa florio became synonymous with  a long and grueling race in the years  after its end tribute targets have  popped up across the world but true  racing enthusiasts know it all began  here  [Music]

